  "summary": "Four new preprints target sampling, model selection, and epitope guidance to improve antibody-antigen structure prediction.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is improving antibody-antigen complex structure prediction by working around the limits of single predictors. AbPoolRank ranks mixed structure pools with a predictor-agnostic consensus, reaching 58.0% Success@1. A separate preprint adds PIPER rigid-body docking templates to AlphaFold 3 and Boltz-2, raising success from 56.2% to 63.4% in a leakage-free evaluation. APEs uses an agentic system that retrieves public evidence to predict ranked residue-level epitopes, guiding complex sampling and model selection. What is new is the shift from tuning a single model toward external inputs and selection layers: docking-derived templates, epitope predictions, and consensus ranking. The SPACE-TCR preprint is heterogeneous to this thread; it groups paired αβ TCR structures by CDR loop geometry to recover antigen-specific convergent receptor families beyond sequence similarity.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-26"
}
